<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/><meta name="description" content="Sarah Whitaker's Bayesian analysis of Studio Ghibli movie revenue."/><title>studio ghibli revenue analysis · sarahwhitaker</title></head>
<body class="night-design project-page report-page"><AnimatedBackground/><main>
<header class="project-hero"><a class="back-link" href="/">♡ back home</a><p class="project-kicker">STATISTICAL ANALYSIS</p><h1>Studio Ghibli Revenue Analysis</h1><div class="floral-divider" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><b>✿</b><span></span></div><p class="project-subtitle">bayesian analysis · R · ggplot2 · monte carlo simulation</p></header>
<article class="report-content">
<section class="report-intro"><p class="section-label">RESEARCH QUESTION</p><h2>Do Hayao Miyazaki-directed Studio Ghibli films have higher revenue than films directed by others?</h2><p>I used a Bayesian model to compare movie revenue between the two director groups, combining prior assumptions with observed data to estimate each group's revenue and the difference between them.</p></section>
<section class="report-section"><p class="section-label">01 · THE DATA</p><div class="stats"><div><b>23</b><span>films</span></div><div><b>11</b><span>Miyazaki-directed</span></div><div><b>$81M</b><span>mean revenue</span></div><div><b>$41M</b><span>median revenue</span></div></div><p>The dataset included film name, year, director, screenplay writer, budget, revenue, genres, and duration. Revenue ranged from about $10M to $274M in the data used for the analysis.</p></section>
<section class="report-section"><p class="section-label">02 · METHOD</p><div class="method-grid"><div><b>01 · PRIOR</b><h3>Gamma-Gamma</h3><p>α = 2 and β = 0.02, giving a prior mean of $100M.</p></div><div><b>02 · POSTERIOR</b><h3>Update</h3><p>The prior was updated using observed revenue for each director group.</p></div><div><b>03 · SIMULATION</b><h3>Monte Carlo</h3><p>Simulation was used to examine posterior distributions and uncertainty.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="report-section"><p class="section-label">03 · REVENUE COMPARISON</p><div class="chart"><h3>Posterior expected revenue</h3><div class="row"><span>Miyazaki</span><i><em style="width:100%"></em></i><b>$104.7M</b></div><div class="row"><span>Other directors</span><i><em style="width:46.5%"></em></i><b>$48.7M</b></div><small>Temporary portfolio visualization based on the original reported model results. Original ggplot figures can replace this when the R project is recovered.</small></div></section>
<section class="report-section"><p class="section-label">04 · UNCERTAINTY</p><div class="intervals"><div><span>Miyazaki-directed</span><b>$99M – $111M</b><small>95% interval</small></div><div><span>Other directors</span><b>$44.5M – $52M</b><small>95% interval</small></div><div><span>Posterior difference</span><b>≈ $56.5M</b><small>Miyazaki minus other directors</small></div></div></section>
<section class="report-section"><p class="section-label">05 · FINDINGS</p><div class="finding">✦ The posterior estimates place expected revenue for Miyazaki-directed films above the estimate for films directed by others in this dataset.</div><div class="finding">✦ The estimated difference is about $56.5M, with uncertainty represented by the posterior distributions.</div><div class="finding">✦ The result describes this dataset and model; it does not by itself establish a causal effect of director on revenue.</div></section>
<section class="report-section"><p class="section-label">06 · TAKEAWAY</p><p>This project combined Bayesian inference, Monte Carlo simulation, statistical modeling, and visualization in R. The final report was designed to make the statistical reasoning understandable to non-technical readers.</p></section>
</article><footer><nav class="social-links" aria-label="Social links"><a href="https://github.com/sarahlouisewhitaker" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GITHUB</a><span>♡</span><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sarah-louise-whitaker" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LINKEDIN</a></nav></footer>
</main></body></html>
<style>
.report-content{max-width:900px;margin:auto;padding:0 1rem 5rem}.report-intro{max-width:760px;text-align:center;margin:0 auto 4rem}.report-intro h2{font-size:clamp(1.35rem,2.4vw,2rem);line-height:1.35;font-weight:500}.report-intro p:last-child,.report-section>p{line-height:1.8;color:rgba(255,245,250,.82)}.report-section{margin-bottom:4.5rem}.stats,.method-grid,.intervals{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:.8rem;margin:1.2rem 0}.stats div,.method-grid div,.intervals div,.chart{background:rgba(8,10,22,.58);border:1px solid rgba(239,180,202,.25);border-radius:10px;padding:1.2rem}.stats{text-align:center}.stats b{display:block;color:var(--rose);font-size:1.45rem}.stats span,.intervals span,.intervals small{font-size:.75rem;opacity:.7}.method-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}.method-grid b{font-size:.7rem;color:var(--rose)}.method-grid h3{margin:.55rem 0}.method-grid p{line-height:1.6;font-size:.85rem;opacity:.8}.chart h3{font-weight:500;color:var(--rose)}.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:110px 1fr 75px;gap:1rem;align-items:center;margin:1.2rem 0}.row i{height:18px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border-radius:99px;overflow:hidden}.row em{display:block;height:100%;background:rgba(239,180,202,.85);border-radius:99px}.row b{color:var(--rose)}.chart small{opacity:.6}.intervals{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}.intervals div{text-align:center}.intervals b{display:block;color:var(--rose);font-size:1.2rem;margin:.5rem}.finding{padding:1rem 1.2rem;margin:.7rem 0;background:rgba(8,10,22,.45);border-left:1px solid var(--rose);border-radius:7px;line-height:1.7}.final{padding-bottom:2rem}@media(max-width:650px){.stats,.method-grid,.intervals{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.row{grid-template-columns:85px 1fr}.row b{grid-column:2}}@media(max-width:430px){.stats,.method-grid,.intervals{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>